From 4f123caa1f696c9d0b1ab93775c49e8007dcdf86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net(v2): adapt V2PeerProtocolHandler, short_id key, and
 MinedHeader to 134-byte V2 headers

Adapt V2PeerProtocolHandler and MinedHeader relay to 134-byte V2 headers
and header state_root verification.

Original-Commit: e112576791cdf3a6d0d935c2f9d7de0fceced62b
Original-Patch: v2/018
Split-Concern: whole

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Retain native header/compact-encoding and token-input network adapters, discouragement API and adapted native wire fixtures. Reconcile duplicate handler/known-transaction interfaces against shared owners and preserve immutable snapshot ownership assertions. Remove deleted legacy blocksnap source from the existing shared target; its peer-handler header capability adaptation in113 must be placed coherently before incremental gates.

Plan-v2 owner repair: Lane B native adaptation: retain the shared reconstruction/selection and unconditional sequence-lock checks while preserving native header, transaction, and state-root behavior.

Plan-v2 owner repair: C native context: preserve one-pass admission and local-origin trickle; retain native transaction/header and prefetch semantics.
